# Wireframe: ConfirmDeleteDialog

## Purpose & Flow Context

Confirmation before permanently deleting an issue. Entry: click "Delete" on IssueDetailPage. Exit: Confirm → navigate to IssuesPage; Cancel → return to IssueDetailPage.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Small modal overlay (400px). No app-shell.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX]                                 |
|                                                                    |
|  +-------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|  |  Delete issue?                                              |  |
|  |                                                             |  |
|  |  "Fix login redirect"                                       |  |
|  |                                                             |  |
|  |  This action cannot be undone. All data will be              |  |
|  |  permanently removed.                                       |  |
|  |                                                             |  |
|  |  [Cancel]                         [ Delete ]                |  |
|  +-------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Modal shell | Modal | Backdrop/Esc = cancel | — |
| Cancel button | Button (secondary) | Close dialog → back to detail | — |
| Delete button | Button (danger) | Dispatch delete action → close → navigate to list | Spinner while deleting |

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| "Delete issue?" | Confirm title — prompts decision | Danger context |
| Issue title in quotes | Identifies what will be deleted | Italic styling to distinguish |
| "This action cannot be undone…" | Irreversibility warning | Plain language, no codes |
| "Delete" | Confirm destructive action | Danger variant, red |
| "Cancel" | Abandon delete | Safe option, secondary |

## States

### Default

Both buttons active. Focus on Cancel (safe default).

### Submitting

Delete button shows spinner and is disabled. Cancel remains enabled. Modal does not close until response.

### Error (API failure)

Inline error below warning text:
```
+-- -------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|  [⚠] Could not delete issue. Please try again.                 |
+-- -------------------------------------------------------------+  |
```
Both buttons re-enabled.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| All | Small centered modal; no structural changes |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `role="alertdialog" aria-describedby="delete-warning"` |
| Heading order | `h2` "Delete issue?" |
| Reading / Focus order | Warning text → Cancel → Delete |
| Accessible names | Delete button `aria-label="Delete issue"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab between Cancel/Delete; Enter = focused action; Esc = Cancel |
| Focus trap | Cycles within dialog; initial focus on Cancel (safe default) |
| Non-color intent | "Delete" button uses text label "Delete", not just red color |
